    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105097" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριοττίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, necklace with <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>three</i> pendants like
			<i>eyes</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίγληνος</span>),
				Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.104
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				976.36
			</span></i>; 
				Dim.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριόττιον</span></b> , τό, ibid.:— a form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριόττης</span></b> , ὁ, is also cited in <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				766.33
			</span></i>; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριοπίς</span></b>  or
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίοπις</span></b>  by <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				5.98
			</span></i>, Sch.BT <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.183
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
